{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[],"authorship_tag":"ABX9TyMEIdldgphvWA09OdsBNm/C"},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Sentiment Analysis\n","\n","## Project Description\n","This project analyzes text to determine whether the sentiment is positive or negative.\n","\n","The model learns from example sentences and predicts the sentiment of new text.\n","\n","## Goals:\n","- Work with text data.\n","- Understand basic Natural Language Processing.\n","- Train a text classification model.\n","\n","## Used Tools:\n","- Python\n","- Scikit-learn"],"metadata":{"id":"q0qcLQvGPHPI"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"wp14Cod928rm"},"outputs":[],"source":["from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import CountVectorizer\n","from sklearn.naive_bayes import MultinomialNB\n","\n","texts = [\"I love this movie\",\"This film is amazing\",\"I hate this movie\",\"This is terrible\"]\n","\n","labels = [\"positive\",\"positive\",\"negative\",\"negative\"]\n","\n","vectorizer = CountVectorizer()\n","\n","X = vectorizer.fit_transform(texts)\n","\n","model = MultinomialNB()\n","model.fit(X,labels)\n","\n","test = [\"This movie is great\"]\n","\n","test_vec = vectorizer.transform(test)\n","\n","prediction = model.predict(test_vec)\n","\n","print(\"Predicted sentiment:\",prediction[0])"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Conclusion\n","\n","### Sentiment analysis is widely used in social media monitoring, product reviews, and customer feedback analysis."],"metadata":{"id":"BDjQlARmPdf3"}}]}